       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg once daily. The usual range is 2.5 to 10 mg. A dose of 50 mg could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Nothing in this patient's profile (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function) would justify it.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, a common starting dose.\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum dose.\n- **2.5 mg** by mouth once daily, for a frail or elderly patient or one who needs a lower dose.\n\nIf you do want 50 mg, tell me the clinical reason and I'll put it in the order note. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
